cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "dualmesh: a multiphysics framework for heat transfer, solid mechanics, fluid dynamics, neutron diffusion and nuclear fuel performance"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
version: 0.2.0
license: LGPL-2.1-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/MohamedAbdulHameed/dualmesh"
url: "https://dualmesh.readthedocs.io"
abstract: >-
  dualmesh is a multiphysics framework for heat transfer, solid mechanics,
  fluid dynamics, neutron diffusion and nuclear fuel performance. Coupled
  problems are solved monolithically by Newton's method with exact Jacobians
  from automatic differentiation. One keyword selects the discretization of a
  problem: the Galerkin finite element method, the vertex-centered or
  cell-centered finite volume method, or the dual mesh control domain method
  (DMCDM). The library is written in C++17 with Python bindings. It is a
  modular framework of physics, kernels, boundary conditions and property
  objects, with uncertainty quantification. It is verified against analytical
  solutions, published benchmarks and other codes.
keywords:
  - dual mesh control domain method
  - finite element method
  - finite volume method
  - fluid dynamics
  - solid mechanics
  - heat transfer
  - neutron diffusion
  - nuclear fuel performance
  - uncertainty quantification
  - multiphysics
authors:
  - family-names: AbdulHameed
    given-names: Mohamed
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-5882-3345"
    affiliation: "Nuclear Innovation Centre, UNSW Sydney"
